        id: "m178980-amggt-fl1", brand: "Mercedes-Benz", model: "AMG GT (Facelift 1)", generation: "C190/R190 (2017-2018)", engineCode: "M 178.980", profileId: "m178980-amggt-fl1", displacement: "3,982 cc", power: "476 hp (350 kW)", torque: "630 Nm", fuelType: "Petrol", cylinders: 8, valves: 32, compression: "10.5:1", yearRange: "2017-2018",
        timingType: "Chain (Located at the REAR of the block. Due to the front-mid engine transaxle layout, the engine is pushed incredibly far back against the firewall. If the timing chain stretches due to poor maintenance or track abuse, accessing the rear-mounted timing gear requires a massive, incredibly expensive engine removal procedure.)", 
        injectionType: "Direct Injection (Bosch ultra-high-pressure system. Highly susceptible to carbon coking. Because the fuel is injected directly into the cylinders, it never washes the intake valves. The extreme heat of the Hot-V layout and track-day PCV blow-by creates thick carbon sludge. Walnut blasting is required every 80,000 km to maintain peak airflow.)", 
        engineLifespan: "150,000 - 250,000 km (Mechanically, the M178 is an over-engineered masterpiece featuring forged internals, a closed-deck block, and NANOSLIDE cylinder walls. Utilizing a Dry Sump lubrication system allows it to survive extreme lateral G-forces on the track without oil starvation. The engine will easily outlast the transaxle and turbo peripherals if properly maintained.)", 
