        id: "m139980-gt43-c192-usa", brand: "Mercedes-Benz", model: "AMG GT 43 (C192 US Spec)", generation: "C192 (2023-Present)", engineCode: "M 139.980", profileId: "m139980-gt43-c192-usa", displacement: "1,991 cc", power: "421 hp (310 kW)", torque: "500 Nm", fuelType: "Petrol Mild-Hybrid (MHEV)", cylinders: 4, valves: 16, compression: "9.0:1", yearRange: "2023-Present",
        timingType: "Chain (Located at the REAR of the engine block. In this longitudinal application, AMG placed the timing chain against the firewall to improve weight distribution and pedestrian safety. If chain stretch occurs, accessing the tensioners requires a massive drivetrain drop.)", 
        injectionType: "Dual Injection (A major reliability advantage. Utilizes both Bosch high-pressure Direct Injection (200 bar) via piezo injectors AND traditional manifold Port Injection. The port injection constantly washes the intake valves with fuel, completely eliminating the carbon coking issues that plague the V8 engines. No walnut blasting required.)", 
        engineLifespan: "150,000 - 200,000 km (ICE) / 6-8 Years (48V System) (The M139 is the most power-dense production 4-cylinder in the world. The closed-deck block is incredibly strong, but long-term reliability is dictated by the highly complex 48V electric turbocharger and the RSG belt-driven hybrid system. The US Spec avoids OPF heat soak, slightly improving turbo longevity.)", 
