            "PCV Valve / Oil Separator Failure: The crankcase ventilation system clogs over time, causing excess crankcase pressure. This frequently blows out the Rear Main Seal (RMS).",
            "MCT Wet Clutch Shudder: The 9G MCT replaces the torque converter with a wet multi-disc start-off clutch. Degradation of the transmission fluid causes harsh engagements.",
            "4MATIC+ Transfer Case Wear: 800 Nm hard launches place extreme stress on the electromechanical clutch packs in the transfer case. Requires frequent fluid changes.",
            "Active Rear Steering (ARS) Actuator Failure: The electromechanical actuators on the rear axle can fail from track debris or extreme heat, throwing chassis codes.",
            "Active Engine Mount Failure: The dynamic magneto-rheological engine mounts leak or fail electronically, causing severe driveline vibrations."
