        id: "m272967-r350-4matic", brand: "Mercedes-Benz", model: "R 350 4MATIC (W251)", generation: "W251 (2006-2013)", engineCode: "M 272.967", profileId: "m272967-r350-4matic", displacement: "3,498 cc", power: "272 hp (200 kW)", torque: "350 Nm", fuelType: "Petrol", cylinders: 6, valves: 24, compression: "10.7:1", yearRange: "2006-2013",
        timingType: "Chain (Early models [2006-2008] suffer from catastrophic balance shaft sprocket wear due to defective sintered metal. The chain stretches, jumping timing and destroying the valves. Requires full engine removal to fix.)", injectionType: "Sequential Multi-Point Port Injection (MPI). The ECU features advanced dynamic adjustment algorithms for the intake and exhaust continuously variable valve timing (sequential VVT)[cite: 1].", engineLifespan: "200,000 - 350,000+ km (Heavily dependent on the production year. Pre-2008 models are ticking time bombs without the balance shaft fix. Post-2008 models are extremely durable.)", turboType: "Naturally Aspirated (Utilizes a complex variable-length dual-stage magnesium intake manifold.)", ecuType: "Bosch ME 9.7 (Mounted directly on the intake manifold. Thermal stress bakes the circuitry, requiring specialized cloning or replacement when it fails.)", euroStandard: "Euro 4 / Euro 5", maxPowerStockInternals: "300+ hp (The 3.5L block is identical in architecture to the 3.0L but with a larger bore/stroke. The internals are forged and incredibly stout.)",
        fuelConsumption: { city: "15.0 - 16.5 L/100km", highway: "9.0 - 10.5 L/100km", mixed: "11.5 - 12.5 L/100km", sporty: "19.0+ L/100km" }, oilSpecification: "MB 229.5 (5W-40 Fully Synthetic - Requires 8.0 Liters)",
        commonIssues: [ "Balance Shaft Failure: Soft sprocket material wears away, causing timing failure (Codes P0016/P0017).", "Intake Manifold Tumble Flaps: External plastic actuator arm snaps, internal flaps carbon up and shatter.", "Transfer Case Chain Stretch: The 4MATIC system's internal chain stretches over time, causing severe clunking under load.", "Camshaft Magnets & Sensors: Oil wicks through failing seals into the engine wiring harness.", "Airmatic Compressor Burnout: Usually caused by a micro-leak in one of the heavy-duty air springs.", "Front Differential Bearings: The 4MATIC front diff bearings whine and fail if fluid is not religiously changed." ],
        vulnerabilities: [ "Catastrophic Engine Failure - Ignored balance shaft wear will lead to piston-to-valve contact and complete engine destruction.", "Intake Flap Ingestion - The plastic tumble flaps inside the manifold can break apart and get sucked into the cylinders.", "ECU Heat Death - The Bosch ME9.7 bakes on top of the engine, leading to invisible micro-cracks in the PCB and random stalling.", "4MATIC Transfer Case Destruction - Worn transfer case chains will snap under the immense weight of the R-Class, shattering the aluminum housing.", "Complete Airmatic Collapse - Failing air springs drop the vehicle onto its bump stops, making it entirely undrivable.", "Oil Harness Contamination - Failing cam magnet seals act as a straw, pumping engine oil directly into the main ECU pins." ],
