            "Electronic Throttle Actuator (ETA): The internal wiring insulation inside the throttle body degrades and shorts out, causing violent limp modes and high idle.", 
            "EZL Ignition Module Failure: The thermal paste behind the EZL module dries out, causing the module to overheat and fail, resulting in a complete no-start condition.", 
            "Distributor Cap Moisture: The engine-driven mechanical distributor cap is prone to accumulating condensation, causing severe misfires on cold, damp mornings.", 
            "Water Pump Bearing Failure: The immense weight of the mechanical fan clutch puts heavy lateral strain on the water pump, leading to premature bearing collapse and coolant leaks." 
