        id: "m104994-s320-w140", brand: "Mercedes-Benz", model: "S 320", generation: "W140 (1993-1998)", engineCode: "M 104.994", profileId: "m104994-s320-w140", displacement: "3,199 cc", power: "231 hp (170 kW)", torque: "315 Nm", fuelType: "Petrol", cylinders: 6, valves: 24, compression: "10.0:1", yearRange: "1993-1998",
        timingType: "Double-Roller Chain (Virtually bulletproof chain mechanism that easily outlasts the engine block. However, the rubber U-seal between the timing cover and cylinder head is notoriously weak, causing severe oil leaks.)", 
        injectionType: "Sequential Multi-Point Port Injection. Bosch HFM-SFI (Hot-Film Engine Management). Replaced the older LH-Jetronic, offering superior sequential fuel mapping but introducing the catastrophic 'eco-junk' biodegradable wiring harness.", 
        engineLifespan: "300,000 - 500,000+ km (The iron block and forged internals are genuinely immortal. The engine is only killed when the biodegradable wiring harness shorts out the main ECU or severe overheating warps the long aluminum cylinder head.)", 
        turboType: "Naturally Aspirated (Relies on a dual-resonance variable intake manifold to boost low-end torque, which is desperately needed in the heavy W140.)", 
        ecuType: "Bosch HFM-SFI (Highly susceptible to short-circuits. As the biodegradable engine harness crumbles, bare wires touch and send voltage spikes directly into the ECU, permanently frying the motherboard.)", 
