            "Catastrophic Head Gasket Blowout - Ignored oil weeping at the rear of the block will eventually progress to a full coolant-to-oil breach, warping the cylinder head if driven.", 
            "Mechanical Fan Clutch Explosion - A seized mechanical fan clutch will over-spin the plastic fan blades, shattering them at high RPM and sending shrapnel through the radiator and hood.", 
            "Water Pump Bearing Seizure - The heavy fan clutch destroys the water pump bearing. When it seizes, the serpentine belt snaps, instantly killing power steering and alternator charging.", 
            "OVP Relay Failure - The Overvoltage Protection Relay solder joints crack over time, instantly killing power to the ECU and fuel pumps at highway speeds." 
