        id: "m119980-s500-me-w140", brand: "Mercedes-Benz", model: "S 500", generation: "W140 (1991-1998)", engineCode: "M 119.980", profileId: "m119980-s500-me-w140", displacement: "4,973 cc", power: "320 hp (235 kW)", torque: "470 Nm", fuelType: "Petrol", cylinders: 8, valves: 32, compression: "10.0:1", yearRange: "1995-1998",
        timingType: "Double-Roller Chain (The chain itself is virtually immortal. However, the upper chain guides are made of plastic that bakes in the V8's extreme heat, turns brittle, and snaps. If not proactively replaced, derailed chain fragments will cause catastrophic piston-to-valve collision.)", 
        injectionType: "Bosch Motronic ME 1.0 Sequential Injection. This major 1995 upgrade entirely phased out the archaic LH-Jetronic and the self-destructing biodegradable wiring harnesses. It introduced modern Drive-by-Wire electronic throttle control, integrated cruise control, and independent coil-on-plug ignition.", 
        engineLifespan: "400,000 - 600,000+ km (The closed-deck Alusil block is an indestructible masterpiece. The engine only dies if the plastic chain guides shatter or if the owner completely neglects the early 722.6 transmission, leading to a drivetrain failure.)", 
        turboType: "Naturally Aspirated (Relies on a massive 5.0L displacement, quad-cam efficiency, and a finely tuned variable intake manifold to generate a relentless, smooth wave of torque.)", 
