        id: "om603971-300sd-w140", brand: "Mercedes-Benz", model: "300 SD Turbodiesel", generation: "W140 Pre-Facelift (1991-1993)", engineCode: "OM 603.971", profileId: "om603971-300sd-w140", displacement: "3,449 cc", power: "150 hp (110 kW)", torque: "310 Nm", fuelType: "Diesel", cylinders: 6, valves: 12, compression: "22.0:1", yearRange: "1991-1993",
        timingType: "Double-Roller Chain (The timing chain itself is highly robust, but it is fatally compromised by the mechanical vacuum pump. The pump's bearing degrades and drops steel balls directly into the chain, derailing it and destroying the valvetrain instantly.)", 
        injectionType: "Indirect Injection (IDI) with Pre-Chamber. Features the legendary Bosch inline mechanical injection pump (M-Pump) with vacuum modulation (ALDA). The pump itself is unkillable, but the engine block surrounding it is critically flawed.", 
        engineLifespan: "150,000 - 250,000 km (Globally infamous as the 'Rod Bender'. Mercedes bored the 3.0L block out to 3.5L, leaving the cylinder walls dangerously thin. The engine ovals its own cylinders, consumes massive amounts of oil, and eventually hydro-locks and bends the connecting rods.)", 
        turboType: "Fixed Geometry Turbocharger (Garrett T3 or KKK). Extremely laggy by modern standards. Early versions were destroyed by the restrictive Trap Oxidizer in the exhaust, which backed up heat and shattered the turbo seals.", 
