        id: "m112922-s280-w220", brand: "Mercedes-Benz", model: "S 280", generation: "W220 (1998-2005)", engineCode: "M 112.922", profileId: "m112922-s280-w220", displacement: "2,799 cc", power: "204 hp (150 kW)", torque: "270 Nm", fuelType: "Petrol", cylinders: 6, valves: 18, compression: "10.0:1", yearRange: "1998-2005",
        timingType: "Double-Roller Chain (Extremely robust chain mechanism. The M112 uses a 90-degree V-angle requiring a balance shaft driven by the timing chain. The chain itself outlasts the car, provided oil changes are done on time.)", 
        injectionType: "Sequential Multi-Point Port Injection. Bosch Motronic ME 2.0 (later ME 2.8). Features a twin-spark ignition system with two spark plugs per cylinder to optimize the combustion burn in the 3-valve chamber.", 
        engineLifespan: "350,000 - 500,000+ km (The M112 block is virtually indestructible. The car around it, however, is an electronic and pneumatic nightmare that will likely bankrupt you long before the engine loses compression.)", 
        turboType: "Naturally Aspirated (Relies on a dual-resonance variable intake manifold. It is desperately underpowered for the immense curb weight of the W220 S-Class.)", 
        ecuType: "Bosch ME 2.0 / ME 2.8 (The ECU itself is reliable, but it is highly vulnerable to catastrophic water intrusion from clogged cowl drains flooding the passenger footwell and SAM modules.)", 
