        id: "m112944-s320-w220", brand: "Mercedes-Benz", model: "S 320", generation: "W220 Pre-Facelift (1998-2005)", engineCode: "M 112.944", profileId: "m112944-s320-w220", displacement: "3,199 cc", power: "224 hp (165 kW)", torque: "315 Nm", fuelType: "Petrol", cylinders: 6, valves: 18, compression: "10.0:1", yearRange: "1998-2002",
        timingType: "Double-Roller Chain (Highly durable. The M112 90-degree V6 utilizes a chain-driven balance shaft. The chain itself is virtually immortal, but the harmonic balancer on the crank is a notorious failure point.)", injectionType: "Sequential Multi-Point Port Injection. Bosch ME 2.0. Features a dual-stage resonant intake manifold and phase-tuned twin-spark ignition (two plugs per cylinder) to maximize smooth combustion.", engineLifespan: "350,000 - 500,000+ km (The M112 block is a fortress of reliability. Unfortunately, the W220 pre-facelift chassis surrounding it is a catastrophic rust bucket plagued by early Airmatic and SAM module failures.)", turboType: "Naturally Aspirated (Relies on variable intake runners. Better suited to the massive W220 than the 2.8L, but still lacks the effortless low-end waftability of the M113 V8s.)", ecuType: "Bosch Motronic ME 2.0 (Reliable engine management, but frequently destroyed by water ingress from clogged windshield cowl drains flooding the passenger footwell.)", euroStandard: "Euro 3", maxPowerStockInternals: "350+ hp (The aluminum block with Silitec liners and forged rods easily handles supercharging, well beyond factory output.)",
