        commonIssues: [ "Harmonic Balancer Separation: The rubber dampening ring dry-rots and separates, causing the heavy outer pulley to wobble violently.", "Crankshaft Position Sensor (CPS) Failure: Fails under heat soak, causing random stalling and hot-start refusals.", "Valve Cover Breather Leaks: PCV breather hoses harden and snap, clogging breather chambers and blowing out valve cover gaskets.", "Airmatic Suspension Collapse: Air struts crack, valve blocks leak, and the compressor relay sticks on, burning out the pump.", "Water Ingress & SAM Module Failure: Clogged cowl drains flood the passenger footwell, permanently frying the SAM modules and TCU.", "Transmission Pilot Bushing Leak: The 722.6 electrical connector O-rings fail, allowing ATF to wick up into the transmission computer.", "Instrument Cluster Backlight Failure: Transformers burn out, causing the dash to go completely dark at night." ],
        vulnerabilities: [ "Harmonic Balancer Machining - If the separated harmonic balancer is not replaced, it walks backward and physically saws a hole through the aluminum timing cover.", "Total Airmatic Failure - A ruptured air strut or burnt compressor drops the vehicle onto the bump stops, rendering it undrivable.", "TCU Fluid Contamination - ATF wicking through the pilot bushing harness floods the transmission computer, destroying it and forcing a violent 2nd-gear limp mode.", "Cowl Drain Flooding - A clogged rubber drain fills the cabin with rainwater, causing $3,000+ in electrical damage to SAM modules.", "Hot-Start Stranding - A failing CPS will abruptly shut the engine off in traffic, leaving you stranded until it cools down.", "Dashboard Blackout - Failing cluster transformers require sending the unit out for a specialized rebuild, creating a major safety hazard at night." ],
