            "TCU Fluid Contamination - ATF wicking through the pilot bushing harness floods the transmission computer, destroying it and forcing a violent 2nd-gear limp mode.", 
            "Cowl Drain Flooding - A clogged rubber drain fills the cabin with rainwater, causing $3,000+ in electrical damage to SAM modules.", 
            "Hot-Start Stranding - A failing CPS will abruptly shut the engine off in traffic, leaving you stranded until the engine cools down.", 
            "Structural Rust Decay - Early W220s suffer from terminal rust on critical load-bearing subframe and suspension mounting points." 
