        timingType: "Dual-Row Chain (CRITICAL VULNERABILITY: Early M276 engines suffer from a severe cold-start rattle. The secondary timing chain tensioners lack internal check valves, allowing oil pressure to bleed off completely when the engine is off. Upon cold startup, the loose chain violently slaps against the guides, eventually causing permanent chain stretch and engine failure. Mercedes issued a technical bulletin requiring the installation of check valves and updated tensioners.)", 
        injectionType: "Direct Injection (Stratified Charge). Bosch MED17.7.1. Features advanced Piezoelectric injectors operating at up to 200 bar, providing incredibly precise fuel metering for 'lean-burn' efficiency. Integrates an ECO start-stop algorithm to reduce idling fuel consumption.", 
        engineLifespan: "200,000 - 400,000+ km (A fundamentally excellent 60-degree V6 architecture, but its lifespan is heavily dictated by preventative maintenance. If the timing chain check valves are installed early and carbon buildup is managed, the engine is remarkably durable.)", 
