        timingType: "Dual-Row Chain (CRITICAL VULNERABILITY: Early M276 engines suffer from a severe cold-start rattle. The secondary timing chain tensioners lack internal check valves, allowing oil pressure to bleed off completely when the engine is off. Upon cold startup, the loose chain violently slaps against the guides. Mercedes issued a technical bulletin requiring the installation of check valves and updated tensioners to prevent chain stretch.)", 
        injectionType: "Direct Injection (Stratified Charge). Bosch MED17.7.1. Features advanced Piezoelectric injectors operating at up to 200 bar, providing incredibly precise fuel metering for 'lean-burn' efficiency. Features an integrated torque distribution management software that works closely with the 4MATIC system.", 
        engineLifespan: "200,000 - 400,000+ km (A fundamentally excellent 60-degree V6 architecture, but its lifespan is heavily dictated by preventative maintenance. If the timing chain check valves are installed early and carbon buildup is managed, the engine is remarkably durable. The heavy 4MATIC system adds significant drivetrain wear over time.)", 
        turboType: "Naturally Aspirated (The 306 hp and 370 Nm of torque provide crisp, responsive acceleration. The 4MATIC system adds parasitic drag, making it feel slightly heavier off the line than the RWD variant, but it excels in all-weather traction.)", 
