        model3DPath: "/images/brands/mercedes/S-Class/W221/w221.glb", model3DScale: 0.18, model3DRotation: [0, 0, 0], modelForwardDir: 0, manualLightPositions: { headlights: { x: 0.15, y: -0.02, z: 0.52 } }, customLightNames: { headlights: ["headlights"], taillights: ["taillights"], drllight: ["drls1", "drls2"] }, author: "Mersedes-Benz S-class W221 (https://skfb.ly/oTZ8N) by Black Snow is licensed under Creative Commons Attribution (http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).", riskRating: 6, lightSettings: { headlightAngle: 0.25, headlightIntensity: 100, headlightOpacity: 0.5, headlightRadiusTop: 0.02, headlightTargetDistance: 4.5, headlightPenumbra: 0.1, meshGlowHeadlight: 70, meshGlowTaillight: 4, meshGlowDrl: 12, useBloom: true }, hotspotSettings: { distanceFactor: 0.6 },
        drivingExperience: "The S 350 BlueEFFICIENCY 4MATIC is an imperious, incredibly stable, and highly refined driving experience. Generating 306 horsepower and 370 Nm of torque, the M276 engine feels significantly crisper and more eager to rev than the older M272. The introduction of Direct Injection and the upgraded 7G-Tronic Plus transmission entirely eliminates the sluggish feeling of the earlier V6 models. The addition of the 4MATIC system, governed by the 4ETS software, provides phenomenal grip in rain and snow, transforming the flagship sedan into an unstoppable winter cruiser. It cruises with near-silent authority on the highway while delivering remarkably impressive fuel economy, aided by the ECO start-stop system in city traffic. The Airmatic suspension maintains the legendary, cloud-like ride.",
        mechanicVerdict: "The M276 3.5L V6 Direct Injection engine is a monumental architectural upgrade over the M272, returning to a naturally balanced 60-degree V-angle and permanently eliminating the disastrous balance shaft failure. However, this early M276 introduces its own highly specific headaches that an owner MUST address. The most famous is the cold-start timing chain rattle; Mercedes forgot to install check valves behind the hydraulic chain tensioners. The oil drains out overnight, causing the chain to violently slap the guides on cold starts. You must install the check valves and updated tensioners immediately, or the chain will stretch and destroy the engine. Because it is a Direct Injection engine, the intake valves are no longer washed by fuel. They will cake with thick, black carbon soot over time, eventually causing severe misfires and rough idling. A physical 'walnut blasting' of the intake ports is required every 100,000 km to restore performance. The High-Pressure Fuel Pump (HPFP) is also a known failure point. Since this is a 4MATIC model, you must also maintain the transfer case fluid; if ignored, the internal bearings will whine and the chain will stretch. Beyond the drivetrain, you still have to contend with the inevitable W221 Airmatic suspension leaks and ensure the cowl drains are clear to prevent the SAM modules from flooding. If the timing chain check valves have been installed, the intake valves are clean, and the transfer case is serviced, this is a spectacular, modern, and highly reliable all-weather luxury fortress.",
        repairCostEstimate: "$2,200 - $4,500 / year",
