        id: "om656929-s350d-inline6-4matic", brand: "Mercedes-Benz", model: "S 350 d 4MATIC", generation: "W222 Facelift (2017-2020)", engineCode: "OM 656.929", profileId: "om656929-s350d-inline6-4matic", displacement: "2,925 cc", power: "286 hp (210 kW)", torque: "600 Nm", fuelType: "Diesel", cylinders: 6, valves: 24, compression: "15.5:1", yearRange: "2017-2020",
        timingType: "Single-Row Chain with Gear Drive (Located at the rear of the engine block. While significantly beefed up and far more reliable than the older OM651 design, replacing the chain, guides, or tensioners still requires dropping the 9G-Tronic transmission. The 4MATIC transfer case adds to the labor complexity.)", 
        injectionType: "Common Rail Direct Injection with CAMTRONIC. Bosch MD1. Operates at a massive 2500 bar rail pressure. Features innovative CAMTRONIC variable valve lift on the exhaust side to rapidly heat up the exhaust gas aftertreatment system. Tightly integrated with the 4MATIC torque vectoring module.", 
        engineLifespan: "350,000 - 550,000+ km (The OM656 marks Mercedes' triumphant return to the straight-six diesel configuration. Featuring NANOSLIDE cylinder wall coating and stepped-recess steel pistons, the core engine is exceptionally durable. Longevity is limited mostly by complex emissions sensors, CAMTRONIC actuators, and the 4MATIC drivetrain under load.)", 
        turboType: "Variable Geometry Turbocharger (VGT). Single twin-scroll turbocharger with electronic actuator. Delivers an effortless 600 Nm of torque from just 1,200 RPM, working seamlessly with the 4MATIC system to provide immense, slip-free thrust in all weather conditions.", 
        ecuType: "Bosch MD1CP001 (Next-generation computing platform managing the complex multi-way EGR, CAMTRONIC valve switching, dual SCR systems, and dynamically communicating with the 4ETS traction management for precise power delivery.)", 
