        id: "m256930-s500-w223", brand: "Mercedes-Benz", model: "S 500 4MATIC", generation: "W223 (2020-present)", engineCode: "M 256.930", profileId: "m256930-s500-w223", displacement: "2,999 cc", power: "435 hp (320 kW)", torque: "520 Nm", fuelType: "Mild Hybrid (Petrol/Electric)", cylinders: 6, valves: 24, compression: "10.5:1", yearRange: "2020-present",
        timingType: "Single-Row Chain (Located at the rear of the engine block. Because the M256 lacks a traditional starter motor and accessory belt, the engine's mechanical layout is vastly simplified. However, the rear-mounted chain means that if it eventually stretches at very high mileage, the 9G-Tronic transmission must be dropped to service it.)", 
        injectionType: "Direct Injection. Bosch MG1. Operates at extreme pressures for optimized combustion. Features a 48V Integrated Starter Generator (ISG) sandwiched between the engine and transmission, providing an additional 22 hp and 250 Nm of 'EQ Boost'. The S 500 software runs more aggressive injector duty cycles than the S 450.", 
        engineLifespan: "250,000 - 400,000+ km (The mechanical inline-six block is a masterpiece of balance and durability, featuring Nanoslide cylinder walls. The engine block will effortlessly outlast its insanely complex 48V electrical architecture. The true lifespan of the car will be dictated by the reliability of the ISG, the 48V lithium-ion battery, and the electric auxiliary compressor running at higher sustained boost.)", 
        turboType: "Single Twin-Scroll Exhaust Turbocharger + 48V Electric Auxiliary Compressor (eZV). The eZV spins up to 70,000 RPM in 300 milliseconds. The S 500 software allows significantly higher sustained boost pressure from both compressors compared to the S 450, completely eradicating turbo lag and delivering a V8-like torque curve.", 
        ecuType: "Bosch MG1 (A phenomenally advanced computing platform. It orchestrates the 48V ISG, the electric water pump, the electric AC compressor, the eZV, and the OPF backpressure compensation. If the 48V system faults, the car is instantly immobilized.)", 
        euroStandard: "Euro 6d (Equipped with OPF - Gasoline Particulate Filter)", 
        maxPowerStockInternals: "500+ hp (The rigid inline-six block is massively overbuilt. The engine responds incredibly well to software tuning, but the highly restrictive OPF heavily chokes exhaust flow. Removing the OPF is physically difficult and triggers massive software faults without specialized tuning.)",
