        engineLifespan: "250,000 - 450,000+ km (The M176 block utilizes Nanoslide cylinder wall coatings, completely eradicating the catastrophic Silitec scoring that destroyed older V8s. The core rotating assembly is bulletproof. The engine's lifespan is instead limited by immense 'Hot-V' heat soak destroying plastic cooling lines, ignition coils, and the complex 48V hybrid network.)", 
        turboType: "Twin Turbochargers (Hot-V Configuration). The turbos are mounted *inside* the V of the engine block. This provides virtually zero turbo lag and incredibly sharp throttle response, but creates a literal oven that bakes every plastic and rubber component on top of the engine.", 
        ecuType: "Bosch Motronic MG1 (Highly sophisticated. Manages the seamless transition in and out of 4-cylinder mode via CAMTRONIC, oversees the 48V EQ Boost ISG, and controls the highly restrictive OPF regeneration cycles.)", 
