        id: "m256930-s580e-phev-w223", brand: "Mercedes-Benz", model: "S 580 e Plug-in Hybrid", generation: "W223 (2020-present)", engineCode: "M 256.930", profileId: "m256930-s580e-phev-w223", displacement: "2,999 cc", power: "510 hp (375 kW) Combined", torque: "750 Nm Combined", fuelType: "Plug-in Hybrid (Petrol/Electric)", cylinders: 6, valves: 24, compression: "10.5:1", yearRange: "2021-present",
        timingType: "Single-Row Chain (Located at the rear of the engine block. Because the M256 lacks a traditional starter motor and accessory belt, the engine's mechanical layout is vastly simplified. However, the rear-mounted chain means that if it eventually stretches at very high mileage, the 9G-Tronic transmission and integrated electric motor must be dropped to service it.)", 
        injectionType: "Direct Injection + 110 kW Electric Motor. Bosch MG1. The internal combustion inline-six produces 367 hp, working in violent tandem with a massive 150 hp (110 kW) permanent magnet synchronous electric motor integrated directly into the 9G-Tronic Hybrid transmission. Fourth-generation hybrid management features complex thermal profiling for the battery to accept incredibly fast 60 kW DC charging.", 
        engineLifespan: "300,000 - 500,000+ km (ICE) (The mechanical internal combustion engine will outlast the rest of the car, as it runs significantly less often than a standard model. However, the lifespan of the car as a financially viable asset is entirely dictated by the massive 28.6 kWh high-voltage lithium-ion battery. Frequent 60 kW DC fast charging generates immense heat inside the cells, which accelerates chemical degradation over time.)", 
        turboType: "Single Twin-Scroll Exhaust Turbocharger. Unlike the mild-hybrid models, the PHEV relies on the massive 150 hp electric traction motor to fill torque gaps, effectively rendering the electric auxiliary compressor (eZV) redundant for lag mitigation. The electric motor provides 440 Nm of instant torque from 0 RPM, resulting in explosive acceleration when combined with the spooling ICE.", 
        ecuType: "Bosch MG1 with 4th-Gen Hybrid Management (A terrifyingly complex computing architecture. Orchestrates the internal combustion engine, the massive high-voltage battery cooling circuits for DC fast charging, predictive regenerative braking transitions based on topography, and the high-voltage power electronics module. A single fault in the HV loop bricks the entire vehicle.)", 
        euroStandard: "Euro 6d-ISC-FCM / Euro 6e", 
